# Auto-requests review from @zerosumpain when a PR touches a protected path.
#
# MIRROR OF .github/protected-paths.txt — keep the two in step. They are
# separate because they do different jobs and cannot share a format:
#   - protected-paths.txt drives scripts/classify-pr-risk.sh, which is the
#     enforcement (a high-tier PR is never auto-merged).
#   - this file is advisory. Required code-owner review needs GitHub Pro on a
#     private repo, so on the current plan CODEOWNERS requests a review but
#     cannot block a merge. See scripts/enable-branch-protection.sh.

